      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px] px-7 py-[84px]">
        <div class="mb-3.5 text-[11.5px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-iris-2">FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="m-0 mb-10 text-[clamp(30px,3.4vw,44px)] tracking-[-.03em]">Questions people actually ask.</h2>
        <div class="faq-list border-t border-white/[.075]">
          <details class="faq-item border-b border-white/[.075] px-1 py-5" open>
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-4 font-heading text-[17.5px] font-extrabold"><span class="faq-plus flex-none text-[20px] leading-none text-iris-2">+</span>Does it work on any streaming site?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p class="ml-8 mt-3 text-[15px] text-[#f4f2f8]/[.65]">On practically all of them. Detection reads the page title and the video player rather than a hardcoded list of domains, so new mirrors usually work the moment they go up. If one doesn't, you can still add the show by hand in the web app.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item border-b border-white/[.075] px-1 py-5">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-4 font-heading text-[17.5px] font-extrabold"><span class="faq-plus flex-none text-[20px] leading-none text-iris-2">+</span>Where exactly is my data stored?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p class="ml-8 mt-3 text-[15px] text-[#f4f2f8]/[.65]">In your browser's local extension storage, on your machine. There is no OtakuList account and no backend to sync to. You can export the whole list as JSON any time, and deleting the extension deletes the data.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item border-b border-white/[.075] px-1 py-5">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-4 font-heading text-[17.5px] font-extrabold"><span class="faq-plus flex-none text-[20px] leading-none text-iris-2">+</span>What happens if a site gets blocked?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p class="ml-8 mt-3 text-[15px] text-[#f4f2f8]/[.65]">Nothing happens to your list. Progress is stored against the show, not the site, so you open a different mirror and keep going from the episode you were on.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item border-b border-white/[.075] px-1 py-5">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-4 font-heading text-[17.5px] font-extrabold"><span class="faq-plus flex-none text-[20px] leading-none text-iris-2">+</span>Will it interrupt me while watching?</summary>
            <div class="faq-body"><p class="ml-8 mt-3 text-[15px] text-[#f4f2f8]/[.65]">Once per show, with a small corner card you can dismiss. After you confirm a series, every later episode is recorded silently, no overlay, no sound, nothing on top of the player.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item border-b border-white/[.075] px-1 py-5">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-4 font-heading text-[17.5px] font-extrabold"><span class="faq-plus flex-none text-[20px] leading-none text-iris-2">+</span>Is it really free?</summary>
